message.content:
This appears to be a CBP ruling on Halloween decorations. Festive articles fall under heading 9505, and Halloween items are classified in 9505.90. Resin Halloween decorations would go to 9505.90.6000 ("Festive, carnival or other entertainment articles... other: other"). Item 9505.90.40 covers "Other: Artificial Christmas trees" or similar. In the current HTSUS, 9505.10 covers Christmas articles, 9505.90.20 covers "Confetti, ...", 9505.90.40 covers "Party favors", and 9505.90.60 covers "Other".

The illuminated cauldron might be classified elsewhere. Illuminated, battery-powered items could go in 9405 as lighting, but the cauldron is a festive decoration whose light is incidental, so 9505 applies. Both items are decorations, so one code covers both: 9505.90.6000.

{"hts_code": "9505.90.6000", "reason": "Resin Halloween decorations (a light-up cauldron and a tree face and arms set) are festive articles of heading 9505, falling in the residual subheading for other festive articles."}
